<section id="creation">
  <div class="wrap dive-phase">
    <div class="dive-phase-label">
      <div class="dive-phase-n">Phase 1</div>
      <div class="dive-phase-when">Roughly the first three months</div>
    </div>
    <div class="prose">
      <h2 class="mt-0">Creation</h2>
      <p>This phase runs like a focused project:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>A core project team</strong> of 8&ndash;12 people &mdash; the sweet spot for efficient, interdisciplinary collaboration, regardless of how large the underlying issue is.</li>
        <li><strong>Executive sponsorship, non-negotiably.</strong> For smaller organizations, the owner or CEO. For larger ones, a country head, division CEO, or regional CEO. Change doesn&rsquo;t sustain itself if it isn&rsquo;t visibly backed from the top.</li>
        <li><strong>Broader organizational input</strong>, typically gathered through targeted surveys &mdash; in past engagements we&rsquo;ve captured input from hundreds of employees to make sure the core team&rsquo;s thinking reflects the organization&rsquo;s actual reality.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>A team-efficiency tool runs throughout the entire process. We never work without one, and for 20 years it&rsquo;s been the same tool: <a href="/hbdi/">HBDI</a>, which we&rsquo;ve used with more than 3,500 professionals across 500+ teams. It gives every project team a shared, more precise language from day one.</p>
