<section id="duration">
  <div class="wrap dive-phase">
    <div class="dive-phase-label">
      <div class="dive-phase-n">Duration</div>
      <div class="dive-phase-when">12&ndash;18 months</div>
    </div>
    <div class="prose">
      <h2 class="mt-0">How long it takes</h2>
      <p>Most engagements run <strong>12 to 18 months</strong>, depending on scope. Twelve months is the minimum we&rsquo;ve found for a genuinely sustainable implementation. The more the initiative requires people to change their actual ways of working &mdash; daily habits, not just priorities &mdash; the closer it moves toward 18 months. As a rule of thumb, 18 months is the realistic minimum for any major organizational step-change.</p>
      <p>It&rsquo;s deliberately <strong>mission-based and time-bound</strong>: a clearly defined goal, a clearly defined outcome, and a clear end date. Traditional strategy programs tend to be broad and need maintaining across several leadership generations; Strategy as a Service is scoped so that a single management generation can see it through, start to finish.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

